#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:290
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The agent reports the files that would move, their size, the new repository and the commit the copy matches, then asks: (1) freeze it in the kept trashcan now, (2) keep in place until the first release, (3) show the file list first. Default if there is no answer: (2), nothing moves. A green fresh clone is the precondition for asking, not the answer. Non-relaxable. Owner ruling, 2026-10-06 (bean 3tza, \"1\"): the host keeps a FROZEN copy in the kept trashcan, not a refreshed mirror and not a deletion; the live copy is the submodule or subscription set up at stage 10."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:123
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The content type's own authoring process runs here, against the staged instance. Many sub-KGs never leave; this task can last as long as the graph does."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:286
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The fresh clone could not be verified. Reported as could-not-check; the in-repo copy is not touched."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:300
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The host consumes the new repository and keeps its own copy, as the owner chose. The cutover can be asked again later."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:215
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The owner creates the repository, or authorises the agent that has the permission to; when that agent is in another environment, the hand-over is one bean and one sentence (agent-handoff). The new repository is read before anything is written to it: empty is a fact to check, not to assume."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:132
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The owner decides, from what is measured, whether the sub-KG starts staging for separation now. Asked as numbered options with the recommended one first and a stated default: keeping it in place is the default, and is a real outcome."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:84
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The person's decisions: whether the sub-KG leaves at all, whether the new repository may be created, and whether the in-repo copy may be deleted. An agent reports and waits at each, asks with numbered options and a default that changes nothing, and none of the three may be relaxed by a package."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:60
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The platform-side stages: pushing generic code and declarations down into the harness below, routing every climb out of the sub-KG through its one import seam, and re-pointing the declaration, the seam and the host's consumption once the new repository exists."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:188
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The rehearsal could not run. Reported as could-not-check, never as green."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:313
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The sub-KG lives in its own repository and the host consumes it from there."
